The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
if (qi.input_buffer_length > 0 &&
    struct_size(qi_rsp, Buffer, qi.input_buffer_length) >
    rsp_iov[1].iov_len) {
    rc = -EFAULT;
    goto out;
}
```
Reason:
This check validates that the total size of the `qi_rsp` structure plus its flexible array `Buffer` of length `qi.input_buffer_length` does not exceed the actual length of the response iov (`rsp_iov[1].iov_len`). Using `struct_size` safely computes the required size without risk of integer overflow on 32-bit builds. If the check fails, the function returns `-EFAULT` and skips the copy, preventing the out-of-bounds read.

